quran[31]{c,v,t}:
  79,16,"When His Lord called out to him in the sacred valley of Tuwa,"
  79,17,(And commanded:) ‘Go to Pharaoh. He has transgressed all bounds.’
  79,18,Then say (to him): ‘Do you wish that you should be purified?
  79,19,And (do you desire that) I guide you to your Lord so that you may fear (Him)?’
  79,20,Then Musa (Moses) showed him the great sign.
  79,21,But he denied it and disobeyed.
  79,22,"Then, turning away (from the truth), he launched struggle (in rivalry against Musa [Moses])."
  79,23,"So he gathered (people) and started calling out,"
  79,24,"And said: ‘I am your lord, most high.’"
  79,25,Then Allah seized him in (dual) punishment of this world and the Hereafter.
  79,26,"Surely, in this (incident) there is a great lesson of warning for him who fears (Allah)."
  79,27,"Is it you who are harder to create, or (the entire) galactic universe that He has built?"
  79,28,"He raised high all the heavenly spheres (planets, after creating them in the infinite cosmos), then moderated, equipoised and stabilized (their composition, construction, functions and movements)."
  79,29,"And He is the One Who blackened the night of heavenly space (i.e., darkened the entire spatial environment like a murky night) and emitted (after creating) the light of these (planets from this space)."
  79,30,"And He is the One Who, later, (after the creation of the planet sun) separated (from it) the earth, flung it with centrifugal force (and spread its expanse to make it inhabitable)."
  79,31,"He is the One Who drew water from the earth (separately), and brought forth its vegetable kingdom (from the rest of the dry regions)."
  79,32,And He is the One Who (putting together different elements) raised from the earth firmly fixed mountains.
  79,33,(He did all this) for the benefit of you and your livestock.
  79,34,"Then, whilst (the universe) attains (to its acme through evolution), there will befall the great all-encompassing calamity (the Hour of Resurrection)."
  79,35,That Day man will retrospect his (every) effort and action.
  79,36,And Hell will be made manifest to everyone who can see.
  79,37,"Then he who transgressed the limits,"
  79,38,"And preferred the life of the world (to the Hereafter),"
  79,39,Hell will truly be (his) abode.
  79,40,"But as for him who feared standing in the presence of his Lord and forbade (his ill-commanding) self its appetites and lusts,"
  79,41,Paradise will surely be (his) abode.
  79,42,(The disbelievers) ask you about the Hour of Rising: ‘When will it come to pass?’
  79,43,What should be your concern in talking about (its appointed time)?
  79,44,"Its ultimate limit is up to your Lord (i.e., as in the beginning, only Oneness will survive in the end as well)."
  79,45,You are but a Warner to him who fears it.
  79,46,"So the Day when they will see it, they (will feel as if they) did not tarry (in the world) but for one evening or one morning."
